     The following kernel configuration options can be used to control the
     aattkkbbddcc driver.  They may be set in the kernel configuration file (see
     config(8)).

     _K_B_D___R_E_S_E_T_D_E_L_A_Y_=_X, _K_B_D___M_A_X_W_A_I_T_=_Y
            The keyboard driver aattkkbbdd and the pointing device driver ppssmm may
            ask the aattkkbbddcc driver to reset these devices during the boot
            process.  It sometimes takes a long time before these devices re‐
            spond to the reset command.  These options control how long the
            aattkkbbddcc driver should wait before eventually giving up -- the
            driver will wait _X * _Y msecs at most.  If the drivers seem unable
            to detect devices, you may want to increase these values.  The de‐
            fault values are 200 msec for _X and 5 for _Y.

     _K_B_D___D_E_L_A_Y_1_=_X_, _K_B_D___D_E_L_A_Y_2_=_Y
            DELAY1 sets the intitial key repeat delay to _X.  The default value
            is 500ms.  DELAY2 sets the key repeat delay to _Y.  The default
            value is 100ms.

     _K_B_D_I_O___D_E_B_U_G_=_N
            Sets the debug level to _N.  The default value is zero, which sup‐
            presses all debugging output.

